.TH MINIOS-CONFIGURATOR 1 "September 2026" "MiniOS Configurator 3.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
minios-configurator \- Configure MiniOS system settings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B minios-configurator
.RI [ --help ]
.RI [ --inherit-cmdline ]
.RI [ config-file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B minios-configurator
is a GTK3 graphical utility for configuring MiniOS system settings. It provides an interface for modifying live-config parameters that control system behavior.
.PP
Reads and writes configuration files in live-config format, typically at
.I /etc/live/config.conf
with validation and auto-completion.
.PP
Categories are directly selectable; this application is not a wizard. A fixed action
bar reports unsaved changes and provides Discard changes, Review changes, and Save
changes. Discarding requires confirmation.
Review output redacts passwords. Saved settings are applied
by live-config on the next boot.
.PP
Requires administrative privileges via PolicyKit authentication.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show a short usage message and exit.
.TP
.B -i, --inherit-cmdline
Overlay supported values from /proc/cmdline. The alternate configuration path remains
the persistence target.
.TP
.I config-file
Use an alternate live-config file instead of the default
.IR /etc/live/config.conf .
.SH CONFIGURATION
.TP
.B User
Username, full name, supplementary groups, encrypted user and root passwords,
and media-backed user-directory link or bind mode.
.TP
.B System
No-root mode, hostname, locales, timezone, boot target, and systemd units or
SysV services to enable or disable.
.TP
.B Security
Security profiles and editable sudo, PolicyKit, OpenSSH, XRDP, X11, password
hint, and screen-lock posture controls. Profile names are not saved as runtime
configuration keys.
.TP
.B Keyboard
Model, layouts, variants, and options.
.TP
.B Advanced
Module mode, additional live-config command line, debug output, and boot-log
export.
.SH VALUES
.PP
\fBDEFAULT_TARGET\fR accepts graphical.target, multi-user.target, and
rescue.target. Short graphical, multi-user, and rescue aliases are normalized.
.PP
\fBLIVE_MODULE_MODE\fR accepts simple or merged. Sudo and PolicyKit modes accept
passwordless, password, or disabled. XRDP accepts relaxed, hardened, or
disabled. X11 and screen-lock modes accept relaxed or hardened. Boolean fields
accept true or false.
.SH VALIDATION
.PP
The application validates host and user names, installed UTF-8 locales,
timezones, keyboard values, systemd units and SysV scripts, conflicting service
lists, and cross-field security rules. User-directory link and bind modes are
mutually exclusive and require a safe path inside writable MiniOS media.
.SH APPLICABILITY
.PP
Hostname, locale, timezone, services, keyboard, boot controls, user-media, and
log export apply after reboot. Account creation, passwords, no-root mode, and
security posture are one-shot settings used only when a new session is created.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/live/config.conf
.br
.I /usr/share/applications/minios-configurator.desktop
.br
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/org.minios.configurator.policy
.br
.I /usr/lib/minios-configurator/
.SH NOTES
.PP
Only explicitly changed fields are saved. Atomic replacement preserves comments,
ordering, unknown keys, ownership, permissions, and extended attributes. Symlink
and non-regular configuration files are rejected. The configurator does not
mutate the running system.
.PP
Passwords are redacted during review and saved only as encrypted values.
.PP
Persistence parameters perchmode, perchencrypt, and perchsize are not
configuration fields. For a boot request using perchencrypt=luks, the
application only reports whether the runtime capability marker contains
luks-layer-v1 at
.IR /run/initramfs/etc/minios-initramfs-crypt ;
it never creates, opens, resizes, or unlocks a container.
.SH AUTHOR
crims0n <crims0n@minios.dev>
